[4.18, "o", "Claude\r\n"]
[4.48, "o", "  The final submission deadline for ARC Prize\r\n  2026 – ARC-AGI-3 is 2026-11-02 23:59 UTC,\r\n  about 31 days from now. You have to join or\r\n"]
[4.6, "o", "  merge into a team by 2026-10-26 11:59 UTC,\r\n  about 23 days from now.\r\n\r\n"]
[4.72, "o", "  The metric is a custom one called the ARC-\r\n  AGI-3 Metric:\r\n  • Each game is scored from 0 to 100%.\r\n"]
[4.84, "o", "  • 100% means human-level performance: the\r\n    agent beat every game using as few actions\r\n    as humans did.\r\n"]
[4.96, "o", "  • Finishing in fewer moves than humans could\r\n    push a score above 100%, but scores are\r\n    capped at 100%.\r\n"]
[5.08, "o", "\r\n  It's a code competition, so you submit a\r\n  notebook, and you get one submission a day.\r\n"]
[9.7, "o", "  Teams can have up to 8 people, and the prize\r\n  pool is $850,000.\r\n\r\n"]
[9.82, "o", "  Everything above comes from Kaggle's\r\n  competition page. The Evaluation and\r\n  Timeline pages may have more detail; I can\r\n"]
[9.94, "o", "  pull them if you want.\r\n"]
